# Title: Invoke-Obfuscation Obfuscated IEX Invocation - Security
# ID: fd0f5778-d3cb-4c9a-9695-66759d04702a
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Daniel Bohannon (@Mandiant/@FireEye), oscd.community
# Date: 2019-11-08
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1027
# Description: Detects all variations of obfuscated powershell IEX invocation code generated by Invoke-Obfuscation framework from the code block linked in the references
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" ((EventID=4697) AND ((regex ServiceFileName="(?i)\\$PSHome\\[\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*\\]\\s*\\+\\s*\\$PSHome\\[") OR (regex ServiceFileName="(?i)\\$ShellId\\[\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*\\]\\s*\\+\\s*\\$ShellId\\[") OR (regex ServiceFileName="(?i)\\$env:Public\\[\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*\\]\\s*\\+\\s*\\$env:Public\\[") OR (regex ServiceFileName="(?i)\\$env:ComSpec\\[(\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*,){2}") OR (regex ServiceFileName="(?i)\\\\*mdr\\*\\W\\s*\\)\\.Name") OR (regex ServiceFileName="(?i)\\$VerbosePreference\\.ToString\\(") OR (regex ServiceFileName="(?i)\\String\\]\\s*\\$VerbosePreference")))
